menuconfig ASTROLABE_FIRMWARE
    bool "Astrolabe dual-sensor trackball firmware"
    default y if SHIELD_ASTROLABE
    select GPIO
    select ZMK_POINTING

if ASTROLABE_FIRMWARE

config ASTROLABE_GATT
    bool "Frozen Astrolabe BLE rotation and input service"
    default y
    depends on BT

config ASTROLABE_USB
    bool "Astrolabe USB vendor HID transport"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_USB

config ASTROLABE_DAEMON_LAYER
    int "Keymap layer activated while a daemon owns the route"
    default 1
    help
      Layer index activated when a daemon claims the route and deactivated when it releases.
      It exists so standalone-only gestures -- recovery holds, HID mouse buttons -- cannot fire
      while the daemon owns input, and so daemon control bits are reported with no arbitration
      delay in front of them.

      The route is the sole writer of this layer. Do not bind a layer behavior to it: the route
      can change with no user action at all (cable pull, daemon crash, keepalive timeout), and
      two writers would desynchronise with no way to recover. Must match the second layer
      declared in the keymap.

config ASTROLABE_LED_PIN_TEST
    bool "Blink the board's GPIO LED to identify which physical LED it is"
    default n
    help
      Diagnostic. Blinks the one LED nice_nano_v2 declares (`blue_led`, P0.15) in three-pulse
      groups so it cannot be confused with the charge indicator or the bootloader's reset flash.
      The SuperMini's user LED is red, so this establishes whether the inherited `blue_led` label
      names the right pin before the real status indicator is built against it.

      Not part of any product build. Enable it on the command line for a throwaway image.

config ASTROLABE_LOG_LEVEL
    int "Astrolabe log level"
    range 0 4
    default 2

endif
